<section class="section-padding bg-light-mint">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="text-center mb-5 fade-in-up">
      <span class="text-uppercase text-gold fw-bold tracking-wider">Help Center</span>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-success">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="text-muted mx-auto" style="max-width: 600px;">Get clear, simple answers to the most common questions about switching to solar energy.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 fade-in-up">
        <div class="accordion accordion-custom" id="faqAccordion">
          
          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-0">
              <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-0" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapse-0">
                What is rooftop solar?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-0" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" aria-labelledby="heading-0" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                Rooftop solar is a clean energy system where photovoltaic (PV) solar panels are mounted on the roof of residential, commercial, or institutional buildings. The panels convert sunlight into electricity, which can be used to run appliances, reduce grid dependency, and save money on monthly electricity bills.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-1">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-1">
                How does solar work?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-1" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                Solar panels contain silicon cells that absorb sunlight (photons) and generate Direct Current (DC) electricity. An inverter converts the DC electricity into Alternating Current (AC) electricity, which powers your home. Excess energy generated can either be fed back into the grid (On-Grid net metering) or stored in batteries (Off-Grid).
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-2">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-2">
                How much can I save?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-2" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                Typically, a rooftop solar system can reduce your electricity bill by 80% to 95%. Depending on your monthly consumption slab, tariff rates in your state, and system capacity, a solar setup will pay for itself in 4 to 5 years, after which the electricity generated is essentially free for the remaining 20+ years of panel life.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-3">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-3">
                How much rooftop space is required?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-3" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                On average, a 1 kW solar system requires approximately 100 square feet of shadow-free, flat, or inclined rooftop space. A standard 3 kW residential solar setup would require around 300 square feet.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-4">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-4">
                Does solar work during cloudy weather?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-4" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                Yes, solar panels work on cloudy or overcast days, but their output is reduced. They require light, not direct heat. A panel will typically generate 10% to 25% of its peak capacity depending on the density of the cloud cover.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-5">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-5">
                How long does installation take?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-5" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                The physical installation of rooftop mounting structures, panels, and inverters usually takes only 2 to 3 days for standard residential setups. However, obtaining government feasibility approvals, testing, and final DISCOM Net Metering synchronization may take 3 to 6 weeks depending on local state utility timelines.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-6">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-6">
                How long do solar panels last?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-6" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                Premium solar panels are built to last and carry linear power performance warranties for 25 years. They degrade very slowly, generating around 80% to 85% of their initial output even after 25 years of operation.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-7">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-7">
                Does solar require maintenance?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-7" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                Solar systems have no moving parts and require very low maintenance. The primary requirement is regular cleaning of the panels (once every 1-2 weeks) with clean water to prevent dust and bird droppings from blocking sunlight and lowering efficiency.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-8">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-8">
                Is government subsidy available?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-8" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-8" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                Yes, residential homeowners and housing societies can apply for central financial assistance (government subsidies) under the prevailing national portal rooftop schemes. Subsidies are NOT available for commercial or industrial projects. Subsidies vary by capacity and state rules, and are subject to change.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="accordion-item">
            <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading-9">
              <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-9" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-9">
                Can solar work during power cuts?
              </button>
            </h2>
            <div id="collapse-9" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading-9" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
              <div class="accordion-body">
                Standard On-Grid solar systems automatically shut down during power cuts as a grid safety measure (anti-islanding protection to prevent electrocuting utility workers). If you need power during grid blackouts, you must install an Off-Grid or Hybrid system equipped with battery storage.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <!-- Subsidy Notice -->
        <div class="alert alert-info mt-5 border-info-subtle bg-white py-3 shadow-sm d-flex gap-3">
          <i class="bi bi-info-circle-fill text-info fs-3"></i>
          <div>
            <h5 class="text-info">Subsidy Disclaimer</h5>
            <p class="mb-0 text-muted" style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Subsidy eligibility, structural processing, and approval timelines are strictly subject to applicable government rules, DISCOM guidelines, and updates. They may change over time. Sky Solar provides assistance in submission but final approval rests with government authorities.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center mt-5">
          <h3 class="h5">Have a different question?</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">Speak directly with our solar engineers for customized advice.</p>
          <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-premium-primary mt-2">Connect With An Expert</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
